# The plugin ships to Unraid (Linux). A CRLF shell script fails there with a
# bad-interpreter error, so keep line endings LF in the working tree too --
# otherwise a .txz built on a Windows checkout produces unrunnable scripts.
# Everything textual is pinned, not just the scripts, so a build is byte-for-byte
# the same wherever it is produced.
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.php        text eol=lf
*.page       text eol=lf
*.plg        text eol=lf
*.css        text eol=lf
*.js         text eol=lf
*.md         text eol=lf
*.xml        text eol=lf
*.svg        text eol=lf
*.cfg        text eol=lf
LICENSE      text eol=lf
NOTICE       text eol=lf
scripts/rc.* text eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.woff binary

# NOTE: the settings page is FanControlPlus2.page. The pre-2026.08.18b route is
# served by a shim that must be named fancontrolplus2.page in the PACKAGE, but it
# cannot be stored under that name here - Windows checkouts are case-insensitive
# and the two would be the same file. It lives at unraid/legacy-route.page and is
# renamed by the build.
